# #5833, C5. Resolving a deferred head refuses when a later raise is already re-claimed
# at the partition, as today's claim decision would: the receiver can never arm, so its
# pin never becomes usable. It edits an operator, not an action.
MODULE: NewbornPinEventuallyUsableDeferredHeadRefusedBelowLoaded
TARGET: NewbornPinEventuallyUsable
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a deferred head below the loaded generation is refused
BOUNDS: WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 0, WithMixedVersion = FALSE

--- FIND
ResolveDeferred ==
    /\ pend' = FALSE

--- REPLACE
ResolveDeferred ==
\* MUTATION: a deferred generation below the loaded one is refused.
    /\ pendGen >= gL
    /\ pend' = FALSE

--- END
